    "b-55-kgr-35-80-2": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-35-80-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The only human-authored regime, deliberately minimized. QA-owned with an enforcement loop that fires on every ship, so a stale standard surfaces immediately instead of rotting. Backing: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "injectable/decomp_standards",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " plus the QA rules. Exists today: yes. It absorbs "
        },
        {
          "insert": "banned_patterns",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "VIOLATES",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " examples attached to the standards they exemplify."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-35-80-3": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-35-80-3",
      "type": "state-shape",
      "props": {
        "description": "proposal",
        "example": "{\n  \"id\": \"standard:decl-style\",\n  \"statement\": \"Declarations are prototype-clean; no K&R declaration tricks to force a match\",\n  \"owner\": \"qa\",\n  \"examples\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"rejected\",\n      \"source_ref\": \"attempt:repair:kr-decl-sweep\",\n      \"note\": \"upstream clang Issues job rejects K&R declarations\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "type": "string",
            "required": true
          },
          {
            "name": "statement",
            "type": "string",
            "required": true
          },
          {
            "name": "owner",
            "type": "string",
            "required": true,
            "description": "QA — enforcement loop is the drift control"
          },
          {
            "name": "examples",
            "type": "array",
            "required": true,
            "fields": [
              {
                "name": "kind",
                "type": "\"preferred\" | \"rejected\"",
                "required": true
              },
              {
                "name": "source_ref",
                "type": "string",
                "required": true,
                "description": "attempt/PR that produced it"
              },
              {
                "name": "note",
                "type": "string",
                "required": false
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "name": "Standard"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-35-80-4": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-35-80-4",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "standards injected at boot (global)"
          },
          {
            "text": "QA rules enforce at ship gate"
          },
          {
            "text": "rejection appends an attempt + a VIOLATES example"
          },
          {
            "text": "recurring tactic HARDENS_INTO a standard"
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-35-80-5": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-35-80-5",
      "type": "interaction-surface",
      "props": {
        "operations": [
          {
            "name": "globalStandards",
            "kind": "query",
            "returns": "injected at boot"
          },
          {
            "name": "shipGate",
            "kind": "event",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "diff"
              }
            ],
            "returns": "pass/reject; rejection writes attempt + example"
          }
        ],
        "title": "What agents get from standards"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-55-kgr-40-30-decision-engineered": {
      "id": "b-55-kgr-40-30-decision-engineered",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "title": "Decision (2026-08-10) — standards are engineered, not extracted",
        "tone": "decision"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Standards are different from the knowledge ledger: they are not dynamically set up by the pipeline. Each standard is deliberately authored and standardized — real thought goes into one because it carries specific lint rules that must work mechanically. The HARDENS_INTO path is human-mediated promotion: a recurring tactic can motivate a standard, but writing one is deliberate engineering, not extraction."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
